gorgias-polus.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P3 (S24): "pain" is taken as the pain felt by the wrongdoer, as opposed to the one wronged in P3 and as the pain the wrongful act causes, by the standard set in S11 and S15, without saying who feels it where exceeds_pain is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S30) does not follow (gorgias-polus.logic.r3.sense1)
gorgias-polus.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C1 (S30): exceeds_evil = F, exceeds_pain = T, exceeds_pain_2 = F, more_disgraceful = T
